  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message about vocalness and weakness",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material (text_chunk_1) which states 'the loudest one in the room.. is the weakest one in the room.' This projection occurs because the meme invites the viewer to identify with the message's implied social commentary — that being loud or outspoken equates to weakness — and to see themselves or others as potentially embodying this dynamic. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the meme's framing creates an implicit identification with the concept being described, making the user a subject of the projection onto the text.",
